    <string name="preset_universal_title">Universal</string>
    <string name="preset_universal_desc">Recommended first. Disables IMS (VoLTE) through telephony shell commands, locks the modem to LTE and turns off the IMS service it detects on your device. Everything is restored when you turn the mode off.</string>
    <string name="preset_stock_title">Stock Android / Pixel</string>
    <string name="preset_stock_desc">Minimal set: IMS off plus LTE-only network types. Works on Pixel, Motorola, Nothing and most near-stock Android 12+ firmware.</string>
    <string name="preset_xiaomi_title">Xiaomi HyperOS / MIUI</string>
    <string name="preset_xiaomi_desc">Same commands as Stock. The hidden network menu is locked on HyperOS, but telephony shell commands still work.</string>
    <string name="preset_samsung_title">Samsung One UI</string>
    <string name="preset_samsung_desc">Also turns off the VoLTE switches, locks preferred_network_mode to LTE for every subscription and disables Samsung IMS packages. On some models the modem drops VoLTE registration only after a reboot.</string>
    <string name="preset_oneplus_title">OnePlus / OxygenOS</string>
    <string name="preset_oneplus_desc">AOSP commands plus disabling the Qualcomm (org.codeaurora.ims) or MediaTek (com.mediatek.ims) IMS service. Confirmed on OnePlus 13.</string>
    <string name="preset_vivo_title">vivo / iQOO</string>
    <string name="preset_vivo_desc">Same approach as OnePlus for OriginOS / Funtouch OS. Not confirmed on every model — try Universal if it does not work.</string>
    <string name="preset_legacy_title">Android 9–11</string>
    <string name="preset_legacy_desc">For phones without the Android 12 telephony commands: sets preferred_network_mode to LTE-only and toggles airplane mode to apply it. Ignored by some firmware.</string>

